within Pharmacolibrary.Drugs.L_AntineoplasticAndImmunomodulatingAgents.L01E_ProteinKinaseInhibitors.L01EK01_Axitinib;
model Axitinib "Axitinib — default model: Axitinib_Tortorici2014_reference"
  extends Axitinib_Tortorici2014_reference;
  annotation (Documentation(info = "<html><body><p>The default model of axitinib: <a href=\"modelica://Pharmacolibrary.Drugs.L_AntineoplasticAndImmunomodulatingAgents.L01E_ProteinKinaseInhibitors.L01EK01_Axitinib.Axitinib_Tortorici2014_reference\">Axitinib_Tortorici2014_reference</a>, chosen among the models extracted from papers (reviewer verdict, ground-truth agreement, completeness). All models of axitinib in this package:</p><ul><li><code>Axitinib_Garrett2014_base</code></li><li><code>Axitinib_Garrett2014_final</code></li><li><code>Axitinib_Tortorici2014_reference</code></li><li><code>Axitinib_Ma2019_PD_tv</code></li></ul><h4>About axitinib</h4><p>Axitinib is a protein kinase inhibitor used to treat kidney cancer, especially renal cell carcinoma. It is an approved medicine and is authorised in the European Union for renal cell carcinoma.</p><p><small>Summary written by glm-5.3-flash from <a href=\"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q4830631\">Wikidata Q4830631</a> and the WHO ATC classification and the EMA medicines list; not checked by a person.</small></p><p>Identity, molar mass and metabolites: <a href=\"modelica://Pharmacolibrary.Drugs.Substances.Axitinib\">Axitinib</a>.</p></body></html>", revisions = "<html><body><ul><li>11/2026 generated by pharmacolibrary-dev export.pharmacolibrary_models from default: parameters extracted from the paper by the pharmacolibrary-dev pipeline, model built by its engineer, reviewed: default</li></ul></body></html>"), experiment(StartTime = 0, StopTime = 86400, Tolerance = 1e-9, Interval = 1));
end Axitinib;
